---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import roomImg from '../assets/images/consult-room.jpg';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../data/services';
const service = serviceBySlug('contraception-consultations')!;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do I need a script from my doctor?', a: 'No. If it’s suitable for you, the pharmacist can write the prescription as part of the consultation. Call us to book.' },
  { q: 'My contraception script has run out. Can you help?', a: 'Yes. This service can be used to continue contraception you’re already using, if you’re eligible. Call us to book a consultation.' },
  { q: 'Is there a Medicare rebate for the consultation?', a: 'No. There’s no Medicare rebate for pharmacist consultations. The consultation costs $35, and your contraception is charged separately. Ask us about the cost of your option when you book.' },
  { q: 'Can I get longer-acting contraception here?', a: 'Not from the pharmacy. For longer-acting options we’ll refer you to a GP. The GPs at <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a>, an independent general practice located inside our store, can talk you through them.' },
  { q: 'Can I get emergency contraception?', a: 'Yes. Emergency contraception is available from our pharmacists without an appointment or consultation fee. Ask at the counter and fill in a short questionnaire. See our <a href="/emergency-contraception/">emergency contraception</a> page.' },
];
---

<ServicePage
  service={service}
  title="Contraception Consultations, $35 | Priceline Pacific Fair"
  description="Start, change or continue your contraception with a trained pharmacist at Priceline Pacific Fair, Broadbeach. $35, in a private room, no GP visit needed."
  h1="Contraception consultations with a pharmacist at Pacific Fair"
  lead="Yes, in Queensland a trained pharmacist can help women aged 16 and over start, restart, change or continue their contraception, without a GP visit. At Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair in Broadbeach the consultation costs $35, takes 10 to 20 minutes and happens in our private consultation room. Please call first, as trained pharmacists are usually available Monday to Friday."
  faqs={faqs}
  hub={{ name: 'Vaccinations & health', href: '/vaccination-information/' }}
  primaryCta={{ label: `Call ${site.phone}`, href: site.phoneHref, event: 'cta_call' }}
  secondaryCta={{ label: 'Hours & directions', href: '/visit-us/' }}
  dateModified="2026-10-28"
>
  <h2>What does the consultation cover?</h2>
  <p>Our trained pharmacists can talk with you about your contraception and, if it’s suitable for you, write a prescription during the consultation.</p>
  <p>For longer-acting options, we’ll refer you to a GP. The GPs at <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a>, an independent general practice located inside our store, can talk you through those.</p>

  <h2>Who can use this service?</h2>
  <p>The Queensland service is for women aged 16 and over who want to start, restart, change or continue their contraception. It became a permanent service on 1 July 2025. If the method you’re interested in isn’t the most suitable choice for you, we’ll explain why and refer you to a GP.</p>

  <h2>What happens in the consultation?</h2>
  <p>A consultation usually takes 10 to 20 minutes. Your pharmacist will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>go through your health and medical history, and any medicines you take;</li>
    <li>check your blood pressure;</li>
    <li>check your height and weight;</li>
    <li>talk about your previous experience with contraception and what matters most to you;</li>
    <li>explain your options and how to use your contraception correctly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If it’s appropriate, your pharmacist can then write your prescription. With your permission, we’ll send a summary to your regular GP.</p>

  <Image src={roomImg} alt="The private consultation room at Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair, used for vaccinations and pharmacist consultations" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px" quality={72} />

  <h2>How much does it cost?</h2>
  <p>The consultation costs $35. Your contraception is charged separately, so ask us about the cost of your option when you book. There’s no Medicare rebate for pharmacist consultations.</p>

  <h2>How do I book?</h2>
  <p>Call us on <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> to book. We have several trained pharmacists, usually available Monday to Friday, but consultations take a little longer and depend on a trained pharmacist being on shift, so please call first.</p>

  <h2>When would a GP be the better option?</h2>
  <p>Sometimes a GP is the better next step. For example, if something in your health history means a method may not be suitable for you, if your blood pressure reading is high, or if you’d like a longer-acting option.</p>

  <h2>Is the consultation private?</h2>
  <p>Yes. Consultations happen in a private room, and your information is handled confidentially. You’re welcome to bring a support person. For other support, see our <a href="/womens-health/">women’s health</a> page.</p>
</ServicePage>
